  "resource_order": [
    "nb_fan_probe allocates the 0x58-byte context with devm_kmalloc before the other managed resources; the encoded flags are 0xdc0, equal to target GFP_KERNEL|__GFP_ZERO. The target gfp_types.h places __GFP_ZERO at bit 8.",
    "nb_fan_parse_dt allocates the 0xa8-byte fan state with the same zeroing flag before hrtimer_init. Therefore the timer callback pointer is null until hrtimer_init, and nb_fan_cancel_timer only calls hrtimer_cancel after it observes the initialized callback pointer.",
    "nb_fan_gpio_proc calls devm_gpio_request first and devm_request_threaded_irq second, passing the allocated context as dev_id. The IRQ handler reads the fan_state pointer from context offset +8, matching the context layout.",
    "Target devres_release_all extracts resources and release_nodes walks them in reverse order. On probe failure, drivers/base/dd.c reaches device_unbind_cleanup; on detach, the same cleanup path releases managed resources.",
    "devm_irq_release calls free_irq. Target free_irq removes the action and calls __synchronize_irq before returning. Thus the IRQ handler is quiesced before the earlier GPIO resource and managed context/state allocations are released.",
    "On normal remove, nb_fan_remove removes sysfs, cancels the hrtimer, and clears the global pointer; the managed context remains allocated until driver-core devres cleanup. An IRQ still arriving in that interval receives the stable dev_id context, and free_irq drains it before memory release."
  ],
  "decision": "No use-after-free or uninitialized-timer cancellation was demonstrated in the reviewed devres path. No source change or status promotion is justified.",
  "limitations": [
